english-language-arts-grade-2 ## Units

| # | Unit and compelling question | Days | Skills | Owned standards | C3 | What students learn | Why this unit, here | Check set adds | Sensitive topics and teacher notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Schools and community. *How are schools around the world alike and different?* | 32 | e2-vowel-teams; e2-fluency; e2-wh-questions; e2-character-response; e2-images-and-text; e2-informative; e2-discussion; e2-spelling | RF.2.3a; RF.2.3b; RF.2.4; RL.2.10; RI.2.10; RL.2.1; RI.2.1; SL.2.2; RL.2.3; RL.2.7; RI.2.7; W.2.2; SL.2.1; SL.2.3; L.2.2d; L.2.2e; L.2.2 | None (ELA) | Topic block: the year's long text, a chapter-length Curio Class story of a girl who changes schools mid-year and finds her place, read whole across two weeks; informational texts on schools in several countries (Curio Class texts with cleared photographs and maps); a poem about the school day. Who, what, where, when, why and how questions answered from the text (SL.2.2 with them); how characters respond to events and challenges (story-map, review); what illustrations, photographs and diagrams add (RL.2.7, RI.2.7); gaining the floor, linking to others' comments and asking for clarification in named protocols (SL.2.1a to c). Writing: the performance task, an informational book on the most important thing about schools, with a topic, facts and definitions and a concluding statement (paragraph-frame and main-idea-details, review), through the process. Foundations block: retrieval and a short placement screen in week 1; the syllable types and the long-vowel teams from grade 1 reviewed (Skills Block cycles 1 to 5); e2-vowel-teams continues in units 2 and 3, where the additional teams are taught (RF.2.3b); spelling patterns generalized and first use of a beginning dictionary; fluency in grade 2 text, read with purpose, aloud with accuracy, rate and expression on rereading, and with context used to confirm or self-correct (RF.2.4a to c), continued all year (e2-fluency, e2-spelling). Lettered parts of these standards taught in another unit: L.2.2a, L.2.2b, L.2.2c (unit 2). | The base text's module 1, six weeks, built for launching routines. The long text comes first in grade 2 because it extends grade 1's