| g1-keep-safe | 1 (days 1 to 6) | A password as a private key, what to share and what to keep private | g2-online-consequences | 1 | Retrieval: share or keep private, three cards |
| g1-split-task | 2 (days 7 to 12) | A bigger task broken into parts, each part into step-cards | g2-algorithm-loops | 2 | Retrieval: split a pictured task into two parts on step-cards |
| g1-change-steps | 2 (days 7 to 12) | A change to the steps changes the result | g2-algorithm-peers | 2 | Retrieval: swap two steps of a game card and say what changes |
| g1-changing-things | 3 (days 15 to 22) | Values that change over time and values that stay the same | g2-name-and-label | 3 | Retrieval: sort four pictures, changes or stays |
| g1-code-sequence | 3 (days 15 to 22) | A step-card plan turned into blocks with one event block | g2-code-loops | 3 | Retrieval: what starts this program? (a given event block) |
| g1-explain-events | 3 (days 15 to 22) | Predict, run and compare for a program that waits for an event | g2-explain-build | 3 | Retrieval: predict a two-block program, then run it |
| g1-fix-sequence | 3 (days 15 to 22) | The debugging method: predict, run, find, fix | g2-debug-loops | 3 | Retrieval: the four words, then one wrong block found in a sequence |
| g1-two-kinds-data | 4 (days 23 to 26) | Counts and descriptions collected by asking, watching and measuring | g2-data-types | 4 | Retrieval: count or description, four cards |
| g1-data-questions | 4 (days 23 to 26) | Questions counting can and cannot answer; questions people in the town ask | g2-data-questions | 4 | Retrieval: sort three questions, counting can or cannot answer |
| g1-patterns-ai | 2 (days 7 to 12) | A partner guesses a new card's group from a few examples | g2-ai-training-data | 4 | Retrieval: guess one new card's group from three examples |
| g1-computing-around | 5 (days 29 to 32) | Devices in the community and what each is used for | g2-interests-careers | 5 | Retrieval: name one place and one device used there |
| g1-then-and-now | 5 (days 29 to 32) | One activity before and after a technology arrived, on the timeline | g2-people-solve | 5 | Retrieval: place two cards on the timeline, before and after |
| g1-people-or-machine | 2 (days 7 to 12) | What people do well and what computers do well | g2-people-solve | 5 | Retrieval: one activity, people, computer or both |

Every row above is named in the grade 2 row's assumes in data/progressions/computer-science.csv, and each grade 1
row names the grade 2 row in its hands_on. The K to 1 handoff is the weak one (STANDARD.md section 2); 1 to 2 is not
marked weak, and grade 2 adds repeat to the event and sequence grade 1 taught.

